            <ArticleTitle>Loin pain-hematuria syndrome with a distinctive vascular lesion and alternative pathway complement activation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1016-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 48-year-old woman with loin pain-hematuria syndrome. Her renal abnormalities included conspicuous microaneurysmal and glomeruloid (plexiform) angiomatous changes. The deposition of both properdin and the C5b-9 complex, as well as the usual C3, in arterioles argues for complement activation. To our knowledge, neither of these features has been previously described. We speculate about the cause of loin pain-hematuria syndrome and note the uncommonness of this entity in the United States as opposed to Great Britain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
